  "authoringNote": "The predicate is failed provenance validation, not access denial or unreadability. The encounter is available and its metadata names the case subject, but the held bytes (a well-formed final encounter body dated 2026-08-20) do not match its contentHash, which is the SHA-256 of separately specified alternate bytes (the same body with encounterDate 2026-08-21); the manifest pins the actual held bytes. Under R09's first-condition order the version is not restricted and the hash check fails next, so its one condition is R09.hash_mismatch, a conflict for the administrative reviewer, naming it as the R09 parent (C07). Its unverified body supplies no fact: no date, practitioner, clinical statement or LCMP flag is cited. No final current usable encounter exists and this version is a current, non-quarantined candidate (C09), so R04 holds R04.encounter_failed_provenance, manual_review for the administrative reviewer, naming it as the R04 parent, with no false absence. R04 reads only final current usable documents (recorded reading of C05 and C09), so it cites the final order's status, date and practitioner identifier (three) and nothing from the encounter. R02 binds the encounter by its metadata subject only and cites the order and receipt beneficiary facts (four). R01 (eight citations), R03 (nine) and R05 (four; the receipt follows the order date span 2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z under C06) pass. R06 stays qualified clinical review with no clinical citation and no administrative effect: an unverified record is not evidence that any clinical fact is absent, and no negative clinical assertion is made. R07 passes with no citation because neither the case nor a current usable encounter states LCMP incorporation; that pass asserts nothing about the content of the unavailable record. R08 passes and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review, from R04 and R09. Distinct from F13x4 (failed-provenance order) and F26x1 (failed-provenance receipt beside usable receipts; R09 hash_mismatch and R05 order_receipt_missing for the second order, not a receipt candidate).",
